---
Fix sample_io uint64 to uint32 truncation.

File size and sample count values read as uint64 are silently truncated
to uint32 in sample_io, causing incorrect behavior for large files.

## Acceptance Criteria
- [ ] sample_io uses consistent integer types for file sizes and sample counts
- [ ] No implicit narrowing conversions from 64-bit to 32-bit
- [ ] Large WAV files (>2GB) either load correctly or are rejected with a clear error
- [ ] Compiler warnings (-Wconversion) clean for sample_io.c

## Test Plan
- [ ] Compile with -Wconversion and verify no warnings in sample_io.c
- [ ] Load a WAV file with >2^31 samples worth of data, verify correct behavior
- [ ] Verify normal-sized samples still load correctly
